<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="044" project="ebilling-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Submission operation and endpoints (SPA + internal)</title>
    <phase>2 Submission and extraction (WP2)</phase>
    <gate>startable</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>New external (CIAM) and internal write routes with firm-scope and core-record authorization, SPE upload and record creation — security-class and the only invoice intake path (ADR-002).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Authorization design across two principal types reusing external-access seams owned by another project; mistakes leak one firm's data to another.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-C</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>013, 040, 045, 029</deps>
    <tags>bff, api, auth, spe, write-path</tags>
    <estimated-effort>2-3 days</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Build one InvoiceSubmissionService with two entry points — an external SPA route under /api/v1/external and an internal route under /api/finance — that validates caller, firm and core-record access, stores the PDF through SpeFileStore in the core record's container, creates sprk_document (type Invoice) and sprk_invoicesubmission (Received), enqueues the InvoiceSubmissionProcessing job and returns 202 with job id and status URL (FR-17). Add GET routes for submission status. Run /conflict-check before the PR (uac-r2 and SPA-r3 share external access).</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expert in BFF endpoint filters, external-access (CIAM) authorization, SPE uploads and ADR-004 jobs. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>Routes exist, are authorized by endpoint filters and gated by RequireEbillingEnabled(); a permitted caller gets 202 {submissionId, jobId, trackingNumber, statusUrl}; other firm, inaccessible core record, non-PDF and oversize requests are refused with stable codes; seeded proofs show the firm-scope and core-record checks are load-bearing; the ArchTest guards are green.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>Spec FR-17, Processing Pipeline step 0, NFR-10, D-24 (internal submission runs the same checks), D-44 (PDF in the core record's general or secure container). Existing external upload (ExternalProjectDataEndpoints.cs:255 matters route, UploadDocumentForParent :1268): two-stage gate Read then Create through the PRIVATE RightsForDocumentParentAsync (:850), server-derived container, app-only upload with ConflictBehavior.Fail, flat file names (SpeUploadPathIsFlatGuardTests), bytes uploaded before the row, owner set through IRecordOwnershipResolver. Note an unrelated existing route POST /invoices/{id}/documents (:368) attaches files to an existing invoice — not an intake path. Firm membership: ExternalParticipationService.ReadOrganizationMembershipsAsync (used at Api/Filters/ContactGrantorAuthorizationFilter.cs:294-304). Submission columns and the firm-scoped alternate key: task 020 (sprk_vendororg = firm, sprk_firminvoicenumber, sprk_channel, sprk_processingstatus, sprk_document, sprk_ponumber, sprk_regarding* fields).</background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Finance/Submission/InvoiceSubmissionService.cs (+ interface, request / result records, JobType constant "InvoiceSubmissionProcessing")</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs (internal routes)</file>
      <file role="new">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalInvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs (MapExternalInvoiceSubmissionEndpoints on the external RouteGroupBuilder)</file>
