  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="owner D-106, refined by D-110 (2026-10-17)">Linked = the record's assigned law firms (sprk_assignedlawfirm1/2) only, and the rule is enforced in the submission service, so it holds on every channel, internal included. The chosen firm must be linked to the chosen core record (matter, project or work assignment). The server refuses otherwise, failing closed, and the picker lists only records linked to the chosen firm.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-91 (owner, 2026-10-16)">The firm invoice number is required on both entry points; a missing or blank value is refused with 400 and a stable code before any upload or write. The tracking number is therefore always set in the 202 response.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-87 (owner, 2026-10-16)">The submission row is created by ITrackingNumberAllocator with its tracking number already set (create-with-number, retry on the alternate key). Never create a submission without a number, never write a placeholder; sprk_trackingnumber stays SystemRequired.</constraint>
    <constraint source="task 020 (2026-10-15)">sprk_invoicesubmission.sprk_vendororg is SystemRequired (a null firm escapes the (sprk_vendororg, sprk_trackingnumber) key). The internal channel must set the firm at create. If the internal channel genuinely cannot know the firm at create, lower the column with Set-ColumnRequiredLevel (scripts/ebilling/EbillingSchema.psm1) and report it with the reason; do not write a placeholder firm.</constraint>
    <constraint source="D-68 / task 022 (2026-10-15)">A firm-quoted external identifier (sprk_externalidentifier) must fill the issuing organization and sprk_regardingrecordid at create: rows with an empty key column escape the D-68 firm/type/value/core-record alternate key and can duplicate. For an invoice-only row, use the sprk_regardingrecordid value task 013 defines.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md §10">Every change under src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api follows .claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-008 / ADR-028">Every route: RequireAuthorization plus an endpoint filter that decides access before the handler; then RequireEbillingEnabled() (the flag never replaces authorization). External routes sit in the existing /api/v1/external group (ExternalCollaboration policy + caller-principal filter) and check the core record with IsOperationPermittedAsync (mutating), never IsRecordAccessibleAsync. Internal routes check the caller's own Dataverse rights on the core record (Read and AppendTo) the way FinanceAuthorizationFilter does.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-10 firm scope">The firm is derived server-side: an external caller's firm comes from their organization memberships; a body-supplied firm id is accepted only if it is one of those (else 403 ebilling.submission.firm_forbidden). An internal caller selects the firm; it must be an active sprk_organization (else 400). The submission's sprk_vendororg is always the validated firm.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-002 / FR-17">This service is the only creator of sprk_invoicesubmission; it never creates sprk_invoice (049 does). Core-ancestor fields come from 013's guard; owner from IRecordOwnershipResolver (RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-007 / D-44">Upload only through SpeFileStore into the container RecordContainerResolver returns for the core record (secure when secure; fail closed); flat file name; ConflictBehavior.Fail. No Blob; this task does not write to the Procedure Library or output containers (028 admits app-only writes to them per D-67, but they are not used here).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-019">Stable ProblemDetails codes: ebilling.submission.not_pdf (400, content type and %PDF header checked), ebilling.submission.file_required (400), ebilling.submission.too_large (413, above EbillingOptions.MaxSubmissionFileSizeMb), ebilling.submission.firm_forbidden (403), ebilling.submission.record_forbidden (403), ebilling.disabled (503).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-004 / ADR-017">Enqueue a JobContract with JobType InvoiceSubmissionProcessing, payload {submissionId}, idempotency key = submission id; return 202 with statusUrl pointing at the GET submission route. Tracking number: the submission row is created through 045 with its number (D-87); the firm invoice number is required (D-91), so trackingNumber is never null.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project coordination">Do not edit Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/** (shared with uac-r2; editing it would make this task parallel-unsafe). Reuse its public seams only.</constraint>
  </constraints>

