  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context and rigor">Declare rigor FULL. Read spec FR-17 and NFR-10, the 013 / 040 / 045 outputs and 020's column list. Re-read EndpointMappingExtensions.cs, ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs and FinanceModule.cs immediately before editing.</step>
    <step order="1">Decide the operation key for "submit an invoice against a core record": reuse finance.attach_invoice (OperationAccessPolicy.cs:184-193) only if its documented meaning covers it; otherwise add one key (AppendTo on the core record) with a comment, and keep OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests green. Record the choice.</step>
    <step order="2">Implement InvoiceSubmissionService.SubmitAsync (validated caller context, firm, core record, file stream, required firm invoice number (D-91), optional PO, channel): validate file; resolve container; upload; create sprk_document (type Invoice, linked to the core record); create sprk_invoicesubmission (Received, channel, firm, submitter contact or user, core-record fields via 013, owner); allocate tracking number if possible; enqueue; on a failure after upload, compensate per the reference (no orphan row claiming success).</step>
    <step order="3">Internal routes: POST /api/finance/{matters|projects|workassignments}/{id}/invoice-submissions (multipart: file, firmId, firmInvoiceNumber?, poNumber?) and GET /api/finance/invoice-submissions/{id}.</step>
    <step order="4">External routes in ExternalInvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs: POST /api/v1/external/{matters|projects|workassignments}/{id}/invoice-submissions; GET /api/v1/external/invoice-submissions/{id} (own firm and accessible core record only, else 404); GET /api/v1/external/invoice-submissions (the caller's firm's submissions for accessible core records, newest first — used by 051 for resume and as the flag probe). Mount with one line in ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs.</step>
    <step order="5">Unit tests for the service (each validation, firm derivation, missing firm invoice number refused with 400, compensation, job contract shape). Contract tests for every route: 401 unauthenticated; 403 other firm; 403 inaccessible core record; 400 not PDF; 413 oversize; 503 flag off; 202 happy path with Location / statusUrl; GET of another firm's submission is 404.</step>
    <step order="6">Seeding proofs: temporarily neutralise the firm-scope check, then the core-record check; show the matching contract tests fail; restore; record in notes.</step>
    <step order="7">Run RouteAuthorizationGuardTests (update the ledger only for these routes), RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests, SpeUploadPathIsFlatGuardTests and OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests; build, full test, publish-size delta; run /conflict-check.</step>
    <step order="8">Update TASK-INDEX.md: change this task's status cell to `✅ [done]`.</step>
    <step order="9">Record deviations (route shapes, operation key, response contract 049 / 051 / 052 rely on) in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If the external core-record or firm check can only be done by calling the private RightsForDocumentParentAsync or by editing Infrastructure/ExternalAccess/**, STOP and escalate (root CLAUDE.md §6) — options: make a seam public in a uac-r2-reviewed change, or a different public check.</trigger>
    <trigger>If an external contact belongs to more than one firm and the spec gives no rule for choosing, STOP and ask before defaulting (current proposal: the request must name one of the caller's firms).</trigger>
    <trigger>If task 020's alternate key is not (sprk_vendororg, sprk_trackingnumber), STOP: a tracking-number-only key collides across firms.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>ExternalProjectDataEndpoints uploads documents under a parent but creates no submission, has no firm scoping and enqueues nothing; FinanceEndpoints covers invoice-review confirm / reject for email-derived candidates. No submission service exists (grep InvoiceSubmission in src finds nothing).</existing>
    <extension>The external upload handler is private and tied to document-only semantics; this task reuses its seams (container resolver, SpeFileStore, ownership resolver, IsOperationPermittedAsync) and adds one service plus two thin endpoint files, as the brief's endpoint-file convention requires.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>FR-17 fails: no server-side intake exists, so invoices would still be created client-side (CreateInvoiceWizard) without firm or core-record checks, violating ADR-002 and NFR-10.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ ; dotnet test</tool>
    <tool name="skill">/conflict-check before the PR</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">Services/Finance/Submission/*, Api/Finance/InvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs, Api/ExternalAccess/ExternalInvoiceSubmissionEndpoints.cs, one line each in ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs, FinanceModule.cs</output>
    <output type="test">InvoiceSubmissionEndpointsContractTests.cs, InvoiceSubmissionServiceTests.cs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">An external caller submitting a PDF for an accessible core record of their firm gets 202 with submissionId, jobId, statusUrl and trackingNumber (always set, D-87 / D-91); the submission row is Received with channel SPA, firm, document and core-record fields set; one job with JobType InvoiceSubmissionProcessing is enqueued.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: external caller for a core record they cannot access → 403 ebilling.submission.record_forbidden; naming another firm → 403 ebilling.submission.firm_forbidden; nothing uploaded, no row created, no job enqueued in either case.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: non-PDF → 400 ebilling.submission.not_pdf; file above the configured limit → 413 ebilling.submission.too_large; unauthenticated → 401; Ebilling:Enabled false → 503 ebilling.disabled on every route.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The internal route runs the same validation with channel Internal; an internal caller without Read and AppendTo on the core record gets 403.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">GET of a submission belonging to another firm, or to a core record the caller cannot access, returns 404 (no existence leak).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Seeding proofs recorded: with the firm-scope check removed, the other-firm test fails; with the core-record check removed, the inaccessible-record test fails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No code path in this task creates sprk_invoice; a failure after upload leaves no Received submission row.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">RouteAuthorizationGuardTests, RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests, SpeUploadPathIsFlatGuardTests and OperationAccessPolicyCompletenessTests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Cover the stated contract plus the edge cases named above. Anything beyond that needs a one-line justification in task notes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size delta of Sprk.Bff.Api measured against a fresh master build and recorded in task notes; no new HIGH CVE.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">dotnet build exits 0; dotnet test exits 0.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>Spec FR-17, NFR-10, D-24, D-44. Shared append points: FinanceModule.cs, EndpointMappingExtensions.cs:376-377, ExternalAccessEndpoints.cs (one mount line; shared with uac-r2 / SPA-r3 — /conflict-check). FinanceAuthorizationFilter has no work-assignment entity-set constant today ("sprk_workassignments" appears in EntityAccessFilter.cs:142). The 25 MB default lives in EbillingOptions (040). The InvoiceSubmissionProcessing handler is task 049; until it lands the job has no handler, so contract tests assert the enqueue, not processing. Done 2026-10-16: new key finance.submit_invoice (Read + AppendTo); external core-record check uses the principal's post-veto rights (Read + Create) because IsOperationPermittedAsync takes a WorkforcePrincipal; firmId is a query parameter; a caller in several firms must name one (400 firm_required). Routes, response contract, seeding proofs and evidence in projects/ebilling-r1/notes/044-submission-operation.md. Review fix round 1: a failed document update and a lost submission-create reply are now compensated. Review fix round 2: writes ignore the caller token (no orphans on disconnect), lost replies and the retried-PUT 409 are cleaned up by path/item/preset id, read faults are 503. rework: fix-round-2 task 044</notes>

